usage: toruk [-h]
             {diagnose,validate-config,audit-evidence,compare-replay,make-fixture,validate,reproduce,summarize,train,evaluate,generate,make-worlds,evaluate-worlds,train-controlled,evaluate-controlled,effect-labels,fit-effect,evaluate-effect,controlled-pilot,verify-m6,generalization,evaluate-heldout} ...

Toruk-LM research foundation

positional arguments:
  {diagnose,validate-config,audit-evidence,compare-replay,make-fixture,validate,reproduce,summarize,train,evaluate,generate,make-worlds,evaluate-worlds,train-controlled,evaluate-controlled,effect-labels,fit-effect,evaluate-effect,controlled-pilot,verify-m6,generalization,evaluate-heldout}
    diagnose            report actual runtime and CUDA availability
    validate-config     validate a versioned reproduction config
    audit-evidence      validate sealed evidence and rescore raw answers
    compare-replay      require exact generated answers and score parity
    make-fixture        generate document-separated smoke-test text
    validate            verify split checksums, config and checkpoint identity
    reproduce           run a bounded foundation or versioned research config
    summarize           verify a sealed run and regenerate result tables
    train               train ordinary LM; CPU; fixed learning rate
    evaluate            local-context loss and autoregressive continuations
    generate            greedy local-context inference
    make-worlds         create frozen controlled worlds and LM exports
    evaluate-worlds     validation-only generated factual answers
    train-controlled    bounded ordinary/recurrent world training
    evaluate-controlled
                        validation-only world answers
    effect-labels       offline bounded paired supervision
    fit-effect          fit effect predictor on training labels only
    evaluate-effect     offline validation effect diagnostics
    controlled-pilot    bounded validation prerequisite/comparison pipeline
    verify-m6           reproduce frozen M6 answers without retraining
    generalization      bounded exploratory M7 held-out failure study
    evaluate-heldout    one protocol-bound M7 cell/checkpoint

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
